# The network of "Replace the VPN": two laptops out on the internet, the
# shop's old VPN gateway, the new access proxy, the identity provider, and
# the apps network behind them.
#
#   laptop   byod      idp (login.shop.test)
#     |        |        |
#   ==+========+========+==== internet 203.0.113.0/24 ====
#        |                    |
#      vpngw .2             zt .80 (apps.shop.test)
#        | .1                 | .2
#   =====+====================+==== apps 10.20.0.0/24 ====
#        |          |          |
#      wiki .10   payroll .11  db .12
#
# laptop is a managed staff laptop with the VPN client; byod is someone's
# own laptop with no VPN. vpngw forwards what arrives through its tunnel
# into the apps network. zt has a foot on each network and forwards
# nothing: it is a host, not a router.
machine laptop
machine byod
machine idp
machine vpngw router
machine zt
machine wiki
machine payroll
machine db

lan internet laptop:eth0=203.0.113.10/24 byod:eth0=203.0.113.11/24 idp:eth0=203.0.113.90/24 vpngw:wan=203.0.113.2/24 zt:wan=203.0.113.80/24
lan apps vpngw:lan=10.20.0.1/24 zt:lan=10.20.0.2/24 wiki:eth0=10.20.0.10/24 payroll:eth0=10.20.0.11/24 db:eth0=10.20.0.12/24

# The laptops send anything for the apps network to the VPN gateway, as a
# VPN client's route does. Only what arrives inside the tunnel gets through.
route laptop 10.20.0.0/24 via 203.0.113.2
route byod 10.20.0.0/24 via 203.0.113.2
# The apps answer whoever asked through the gateway.
route wiki default via 10.20.0.1
route payroll default via 10.20.0.1
route db default via 10.20.0.1

run idp keycloak
run vpngw strongswan nftables
run laptop strongswan
run zt nginx
run wiki nginx
run payroll nginx
